mapping "W5409.1" source="W5409" target="37383006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W5409 SNOMED CT 37383006 is a Swedish national extension of ICD-10 W54 (Bitten or struck by
        dog) that adds circumstantial place (residential home/area) and activity (unspecified) context.
        The base ICD-10 W54 concept exists in the Athena mirror (concept_id 45756305) and has a verified
        crosswalk to SNOMED CT 4291007 (concept_code 37383006). Target 4291007 is broader: it subsumes all
        mammal-attack exposures including dog bites/strikes, fully containing the clinical-injury core
        of the source. The place/activity context the Swedish extension encodes has no representation in
        any standard vocabulary and is circumstantial metadata, not a separate clinical concept, so
        broader (not partial) applies. Confidence (moderate): Athena crosswalk verified at the W54 level
        but applied to a Swedish-extension sub-code with additional context not captured, and the target
        climbs two levels (dog → mammal).
        """
}
